WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:08.170
It’s been an exciting couple of months in
Kaiapoi’s Regeneration areas.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:12.210
Earlier this month, the new Community BMX
track was officially opened.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.710
There was a great turnout from keen riders,
both young and old, who lined up try out the track.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:24.039
The opening had been highly anticipated
and the ribbon was cut by Olympian Trent Jones,

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:26.960
who designed and built the track.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.189
Designing the track, I wanted to be able to
cater for a wider audience of cycling and

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:36.559
BMX, and that stemmed from beginners who have
never ridden a BMX track before, all the way

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:39.260
to myself who has been fully professional.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:45.519
Many of the people attending, including Trent,
were members of the old Kaiapoi BMX club.

00:00:45.519 --> 00:00:50.839
They lost their club track as a result of
damage caused by September 2010 earthquake.

00:00:50.839 --> 00:00:55.769
It’s kinda cool to be able to build this
one and reinstate a BMX track here after growing

00:00:55.769 --> 00:00:58.460
up in Kaiapoi riding the tracks.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:04.339
In the Town Centre, the Kaiapoi Marine Precinct
is now open for business, following dredging

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:09.530
over winter and the installation of the final
112 metre floating pontoon.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:14.840
The Council has already received several applications
for long-term berths.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:21.880
Space has also been set aside for casual and
short-term use, and for the River Queen.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.880
The Kaiapoi Dog Park is also nearly ready,
with the walking tracks, fences,

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.160
and gates all complete.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.280
It has separate areas for small and large
dogs, and is expected to open to the public

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.799
in a few weeks’ time once the grass is fully
established.

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:42.759
Next door, a recent Community Planting Day
saw residents and visitors planting another

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.480
600 native seedlings in the Honda Forrest.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.240
The Regeneration focus now turns towards the
sports fields, with tenders recently sought

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.600
for the construction of the changing facilities,
softball diamonds and surrounding roads.

